<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss construction spending seen falling in 1997.</title>
<headline>Swiss construction spending seen falling in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Construction spending in Switzerland is expected to fall a nominal 11.8 percent in 1997 after slumping 13.5 percent in 1996 to 40.39 billion Swiss francs, according to provisional figures compiled by the Federal Statistics Office.</p>
<p>    It gave these figures:	    96/95			97/96</p>
<p> (in million Swiss francs) 1996   pct change  1997 plan  pct chg</p>
<p> Total			  40,386    -13.5	41,809     -11.8</p>
<p> Public maintenance	  2,832    + 0.4	 3,046     + 1.4</p>
<p> New construction	   23,831    -19.8	26,245     -16.6</p>
<p> Renovation		   13,723    - 3.0	12,518     - 3.3</p>
<p>NOTE - The 1996 decline was around 10 percent in real terms on the basis of estimated construction sector deflation of 3.5 percent. The 1997 figures refer to announced plans. The percentage change refers to 1996 announced plans.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
